    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-1126",
      "problem": "The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below. Given that $f$ is periodic with period $4$, what is the value of $f(84)?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14230523/assets/b763649968dc1a117007eba0b7cb0862473aadf702e8c91fc30ac83149445865.png)",
      "worked_solution": "Since the period is $4,$ if we add (or subtract) any multiple of $4$ from the input, the output stays the same.\n\nSo, we can keep subtracting $4$ from the input until we get to an input that we see in the graph:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(84) & =f(84-4) \\\\  & =f(84-2\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =⋯ \\\\  & =f(84-20\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =f(4) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14230523/observations/step-e1126-31683a60374ab88ccffc.html",
